.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 435 AM PDT Sun Aug 16 2026

IFR to LIFR conditions are being observed across the Bay Area and
Monterey Peninsula thanks to a compressing marine layer. LIFR CIGs
are most likely directly along the coast while confidence is
slightly higher in IFR CIGs across the interior. With the
compressing marine layer there is some potential for fog to
develop along the coast and North Bay Valleys. Models are in good
agreement that conditions will improve by 18-19Z which should be
slightly earlier than yesterday. Breezy afternoon winds weaken
overnight, becoming light and variable. Widespread stratus is
expected again tonight with IFR-LIFR CIGs returning. Moderate
confidence that there will be reductions in visibility along the
coast tonight with some potential for fog.

Vicinity of SFO...IFR CIGs continue through late this morning with
a low (20-30%) chance of LIFR CIGs at least briefly developing
this morning. Stratus is expected to clear by late morning before
returning again this evening. Current thinking is that CIGs will
gradually lower from MVFR to IFR overnight. Breezy onshore winds
expected during the day with light, offshore at times, winds
expected overnight.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...IFR-LIFR CIGs continue this morning with
some potential for fog to develop through 16/17Z. CIGs clear at
SNS by late morning but confidence is lower that ceilings will
clear at MRY today. Guidance shows stratus lingering along the
coast with MRY just on the edge of it today. Opted for a less
optimistic TAF with stratus persisting at MRY through the day.
Otherwise, stratus returns by the early evening with ceilings
lowering to IFR-LIFR. LIFR CIGs are more likely given the
compressing marine layer.

